{"status":"confirmed","reasoning":"The hypotenuse is 2\\sqrt{6}, so the legs satisfy a^2+b^2=24. Thus A=ab/2≤(a^2+b^2)/4=6, with equality when both legs equal 2\\sqrt{3}. This agrees with the earlier answer, the submitted value graded Correct, and Math Academy's worked solution.","confidence":1,"answers":[{"key":"field-1","correct_value":"6","correct_option":null,"value_type":"math","wrong_value":"12","correct_keys":[],"wrong_keys":[],"ma_value":"6","ma_basis":"worked_solution","ma_evidence":"\\begin{aligned}{A}_{\\text{max}}=A(2\\sqrt{3}) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{24-(2\\sqrt{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{24-12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}","disagrees":false}]}